From 7fa7ec74a0cae26e130955e5260fe1db1d7492d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:56:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 114/147] rtc: interface: Release the wakeup source when
 reading the time fails

rtc_set_time(), rtc_update_irq() and rtc_timer_enqueue() take the RTC's
wakeup source with pm_stay_awake() and hand over to rtc_timer_do_work(),
which releases it at its end. When reading the time fails there, it
returns early and the wakeup source stays active forever.

On a Surface Duo 2 the EFI RTC (rtc0) cannot be read (the firmware
returns an error): rtc-efi.0 was active from boot on, counting about 27
events a second. An active wakeup source makes every read of
/sys/power/wakeup_count block, so a user space suspend daemon could not
use it.

Release the wakeup source on that path too.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/rtc/interface.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/interface.c b/drivers/rtc/interface.c
index 96626f8068f9..59fbbafb076c 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/interface.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/interface.c
@@ -980,6 +980,8 @@ void rtc_timer_do_work(struct work_struct *work)
 again:
 	err = __rtc_read_time(rtc, &tm);
 	if (err) {
+		/* the callers' pm_stay_awake() must not be left active */
+		pm_relax(rtc->dev.parent);
 		mutex_unlock(&rtc->ops_lock);
 		return;
 	}
